title: WhatMunirHas
---
<<SetShot "Wide">>
Prince: Night in the hospital. Machines hummin’ in the dark.
Prince: Munir left about an hour ago. He always leaves late.
Prince: The old man in the bed beside mine is asleep.
Prince: Can’t move. Can’t speak. Just breathin’.
Prince: And I can’t shut my eyes.
Prince: No energy drink in here. Nothin’ to fix. Nothin’ to check.
Prince: Back home I’d be walkin’ the hideout right now.
Prince: Doors. Windows. The kids. Every last one.
Prince: Here I just gotta sit with my own head.
Prince: And I keep seein’ him.
<<SetShot "CloseUp_A">>
Prince: How does someone become like that?
Prince: First off — the way he is with his old man.
Prince: Comes every day. Same time, rain or not.
Prince: Sits for hours by a father who can’t answer him.
Prince: Nobody’s watchin’. Nobody’s takin’ notes.
Prince: His old man ain’t gonna pay him back. Can’t.
Prince: I never seen a man serve somebody like that.
Prince: Back where I’m from, everybody counts what they give.
Prince: You scratch my back, I scratch yours. That’s the deal.
Prince: He don’t even seem to be countin’.
<<SetShot "Wide">>
Prince: And he ain’t just good to his people, either.
Prince: Every nurse gets a word from him.
Prince: The old guy in the hall. The kid with the broken arm.
Prince: Me. Some stranger in a bed.
Prince: He talks to me like I’m somebody.
Prince: Same manners. No exceptions.
Prince: I been runnin’ a crew of twenty kids for a while now.
Prince: I don’t hand out that kind of respect for free.
Prince: He hands it to every soul he passes.
<<SetShot "CloseUp_A">>
Prince: Then there’s the size of him.
Prince: Biggest man I ever seen. Like a mountain standin’.
Prince: Could clear this whole ward with one hand, probably.
Prince: Never once used it.
Prince: Moves like he’s scared of breakin’ somethin’.
Prince: Trains too. Lifts. Hikes. Keeps his back straight.
Prince: Discipline you can see from across the room.
Prince: A man that strong could take anythin’ he wanted.
Prince: He just don’t. That’s the part that gets me.
<<SetShot "Wide">>
Prince: And the kids. Five kids.
Prince: Three sons, two daughters. His oldest is twelve.
Prince: He talks about ’em like they’re his best work.
Prince: Never raises his voice with ’em. Never rushes.
Prince: “Patience is a language I learned at home.”
Prince: He says it like it’s nothin’. Like it’s free.
Prince: I always figured I’d be a father someday.
Prince: Twenty kids look to me already. Mine. I built that.
Prince: But I built it outta fear. Outta need.
Prince: He built his outta patience. Same job. Different hands.
<<SetShot "CloseUp_A">>
Prince: And he leads. Whole community leans on him.
Prince: I seen people rest when he walks in the room.
Prince: That’s my job too. Keep the lights on. Keep walls up.
Prince: I built a warehouse into a home with my own hands.
Prince: But my crew follows me ‘cause there ain’t nobody else.
Prince: His neighborhood follows him ‘cause they wanna.
Prince: A leader who serves. I never heard of that before.
Prince: And underneath all of it, he’s content.
Prince: Don’t chase. Don’t complain. Don’t run from quiet.
Prince: Carried his father since he was thirteen. No bitterness.
Prince: Not one drop. Sits in that silence like it’s home.
Prince: I can’t do quiet. Quiet’s where the thoughts live.
Prince: Soon as it gets still, my head starts runnin’.
Prince: The two years. The gang. The ones I couldn’t keep.
Prince: He sits in the same quiet and it just rests on him.
Prince: And he keeps his word. That might be the rarest one.
Prince: Same hour, every single day. Ain’t missed one yet.
Prince: What he says is gonna happen, happens.
Prince: In my world, words are cheap. Plans change. Men fold.
Prince: He says it, and it’s already true.
<<SetShot "Wide">>
Prince: I kept tellin’ myself it was luck.
Prince: Some men get dealt a good hand and call it a life.
Prince: But that ain’t it. This ain’t luck.
<<wait>>
Prince: He’s buildin’ from plans. Real ones.
Prince: Every piece of him lines up.
Prince: The care. The manners. The strength. The family.
Prince: The calm. The word he keeps.
Prince: None of that’s a mood. None of that’s a good day.
Prince: That’s a foundation. Laid on purpose.
Prince: Heh. …I never even met a man who was tryin’.
<<SetShot "CloseUp_A">>
Prince: And I want it.
Prince: Not the stuff. Not the job. Not the size.
Prince: I want the foundation.
Prince: I wanna understand him.
Prince: Who gave him the plans. How he learned to build.
Prince: When I get outta here, I’m findin’ him.
Prince: First thing. Before anythin’ else.
Prince: Two years. And I finally know the next step.
Prince: This place was supposed to be where it ended.
Prince: Where my clock started runnin’ out.
Prince: But I keep thinkin’ about him.
Prince: About what he’s got. What I’m gonna learn.
Prince: Maybe there’s another way to live.
Prince: …I gotta find out.
===
